---
import EditorialLayout from "../layouts/EditorialLayout.astro";
import "../styles/pages/index.css";
---

<EditorialLayout
  title={"Custom Clothing Manufacturers - YAUUM"}
  description={"Yauum helps B2B menswear and streetwear buyers develop hoodies, T-shirts, jackets, pants, sportswear, labels, samples, and bulk orders with controlled sampling, fit review, private label execution, quality checks, and shipment-ready packing."}
  canonical="https://yauum.com/"
  variant="home"
  navCurrent={["/"]}
>
<!-- ============ 2 HERO ============ -->
<section class="hero" data-od-id="homepage-hero">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="label">B2B / Private label / OEM-ODM</p>
        <h1>Custom clothing manufacturing, made clear before bulk.</h1>
        <p class="lead hero-lead">Yauum helps overseas apparel brands, wholesalers, sourcing teams, and procurement buyers develop menswear and streetwear through a sample-first workflow: from product brief and material review to private label finishing, inspection, and shipment preparation.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button" href="/contact-us/">Send your product brief</a>
          <a class="link" href="/production/">Review the production path</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-media">
        <img src="/uploads/factory/factory-sewing-line-wide.webp" alt="Garment sewing line with operators and workstations" width="2400" height="1600" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" />
      </div>
      <div class="hero-rail" aria-label="Manufacturing workflow summary">
        <span class="rail-item"><span class="rail-num">01</span><span class="rail-label">Product scope</span></span>
        <span class="rail-item"><span class="rail-num">02</span><span class="rail-label">Sample before bulk</span></span>
        <span class="rail-item"><span class="rail-num">03</span><span class="rail-label">Inspection and pack-out</span></span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 3 MANUFACTURER VALUE ============ -->
<section class="section band-alt" data-od-id="buyer-value-proposition">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="value-grid">
      <div class="value-title" data-reveal>
        <p class="label">Manufacturer value</p>
        <h2>A supplier should make every product decision easier to verify.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="value-body" data-reveal>
        <p class="lead">Yauum supports B2B menswear and streetwear development, sampling, private label execution, quality checks, packing, and shipment preparation.</p>
        <a class="link" href="/our-services/">See manufacturing services</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="buyer-grid" aria-label="Buyer types">
      <article class="buyer-cell">
        <span class="label">BUYER / 01</span>
        <h3>Apparel brands</h3>
        <p>Develop one focused product group, approve the sample, and define brand finishing before bulk.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="buyer-cell">
        <span class="label">BUYER / 02</span>
        <h3>Wholesalers</h3>
        <p>Use approved measurements, packing rules, and order references to support repeat production.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="buyer-cell">
        <span class="label">BUYER / 03</span>
        <h3>Sourcing teams</h3>
        <p>Review materials, construction, artwork, labels, inspection points, and shipment preparation in one workflow.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="buyer-cell">
        <span class="label">BUYER / 04</span>
        <h3>Procurement</h3>
        <p>Send clear specifications and assess the manufacturing path before committing an order.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 4 PRODUCT CATEGORIES ============ -->
<section class="section" id="product-categories" data-od-id="product-categories">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="cat-head">
      <div class="cat-title" data-reveal>
        <p class="label">Product categories</p>
        <h2>Six core categories. One controlled development path.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="cat-note" data-reveal>
        <p class="lead">Choose the product family first, then move through the same structured path for materials, workmanship, branding, checking, packing, and delivery inputs.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="cat-grid">
      <a class="cat-card" href="/hoodie-manufacturer/" data-reveal>
        <span class="cat-media"><img src="/uploads/products/hoodie-manufacturer.webp" alt="Hoodie Manufacturer product reference" width="844" height="1448" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span>
        <span class="cat-meta"><span class="cat-num">01</span><h3>Hoodie</h3></span>
        <p>Pullover and related hoodie programs with fabric, fit, graphics, embroidery, labels, trims, and packaging coordination.</p>
        <span class="link">Review scope</span>
      </a>
      <a class="cat-card" href="/t-shirt-manufacturer/" data-reveal>
        <span class="cat-media"><img src="/uploads/products/t-shirt-manufacturer.webp" alt="T-Shirt Manufacturer product reference" width="844" height="1448" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span>
        <span class="cat-meta"><span class="cat-num">02</span><h3>T-Shirt</h3></span>
        <p>Fabric and fit planning, print-method selection, neck and care labels, hangtags, folding, and packaging.</p>
        <span class="link">Review scope</span>
      </a>
      <a class="cat-card" href="/jackets-manufacturer/" data-reveal>
        <span class="cat-media"><img src="/uploads/products/jackets-manufacturer.webp" alt="Jackets Manufacturer product reference" width="844" height="1448" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span>
        <span class="cat-meta"><span class="cat-num">03</span><h3>Jackets</h3></span>
        <p>Shell, lining, closures, hardware, pockets, branding, labels, and pack-out planned as one outerwear system.</p>
        <span class="link">Review scope</span>
      </a>
      <a class="cat-card" href="/pants-manufacturer/" data-reveal>
        <span class="cat-media"><img src="/uploads/products/pants-manufacturer.webp" alt="Pants Manufacturer product reference" width="844" height="1448" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span>
        <span class="cat-meta"><span class="cat-num">04</span><h3>Pants</h3></span>
        <p>Cargo, jogger, casual, and related programs shaped by fit, pockets, reinforcement, trims, labels, and washing.</p>
        <span class="link">Review scope</span>
      </a>
      <a class="cat-card" href="/sportswear-manufacturer/" data-reveal>
        <span class="cat-media"><img src="/uploads/products/sportswear-manufacturer.webp" alt="Sportswear Manufacturer product reference" width="844" height="1448" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span>
        <span class="cat-meta"><span class="cat-num">05</span><h3>Sportswear</h3></span>
        <p>Stretch-fabric and activewear programs with construction, reflective details, labels, and packaging review.</p>
        <span class="link">Review scope</span>
      </a>
      <a class="cat-card" href="/streetwear-manufacturer/" data-reveal>
        <span class="cat-media"><img src="/uploads/products/streetwear-manufacturer.webp" alt="Streetwear Manufacturer product reference" width="844" height="1448" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span>
        <span class="cat-meta"><span class="cat-num">06</span><h3>Streetwear</h3></span>
        <p>Fit-led product development with graphics, embroidery, patches, washes, trims, private labels, and packaging.</p>
        <span class="link">Review scope</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 5 FROM BRIEF TO BULK ============ -->
<section class="section band-dark" data-od-id="production-process">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="proc-head">
      <div class="p-title" data-reveal>
        <p class="label label--onDark">From brief to bulk</p>
        <h2>Make the order clear before production starts.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="p-note" data-reveal>
        <p class="lead">Each stage turns buyer input into a reference for the next stage. The approved sample becomes the basis for bulk manufacturing.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <ol class="proc">
      <li class="proc-step" data-reveal>
        <span class="proc-num">01</span>
        <h3>Send the product details</h3>
        <p>Share the category, quantity, target market, size range, price target, reference photos or tech pack, fabric idea, labels, packing needs, and delivery plan.</p>
        <span class="proc-out">Output / Initial requirement set</span>
      </li>
      <li class="proc-step" data-reveal>
        <span class="proc-num">02</span>
        <h3>Confirm materials and workmanship</h3>
        <p>Review fabric weight and composition, color, handfeel, buttons, zippers, drawcords, stitching, lining, artwork, decoration, labels, and packaging.</p>
        <span class="proc-out">Output / Agreed product specification</span>
      </li>
      <li class="proc-step" data-reveal>
        <span class="proc-num">03</span>
        <h3>Make and review the sample</h3>
        <p>Check fit, measurements, construction, fabric behavior, artwork placement, trims, brand details, and the overall product before bulk.</p>
        <span class="proc-out">Output / Sample comments and revisions</span>
      </li>
      <li class="proc-step" data-reveal>
        <span class="proc-num">04</span>
        <h3>Approve or revise</h3>
        <p>Adjust the measurements, materials, labels, artwork placement, packing, or finishing until both sides have the production reference.</p>
        <span class="proc-out">Output / Approved sample standard</span>
      </li>
      <li class="proc-step" data-reveal>
        <span class="proc-num">05</span>
        <h3>Produce, check, and pack</h3>
        <p>Bulk work follows the approved sample through cutting, sewing, decoration, finishing, inspection, folding, packing, and shipment preparation.</p>
        <span class="proc-out">Output / Shipment-ready order references</span>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 6 PRODUCTION EVIDENCE ============ -->
<section class="section" data-od-id="factory-capability">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="evidence-grid">
      <figure class="evidence-media" data-reveal>
        <img src="/uploads/factory/factory-cutting.webp" alt="Fabric cutting table and cutting equipment in a garment production area" width="2400" height="1600" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <figcaption class="evidence-cap"><strong>Supplied factory reference /</strong> Visible cutting tables and production equipment. Capacity, location, ownership, and certifications remain to be confirmed.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="evidence-body" data-reveal>
        <p class="label">Factory evidence</p>
        <h2>Show the production work, not unsupported factory promises.</h2>
        <p class="lead">This prototype makes room for real production-floor, sample-room, equipment, inspection, and packing evidence. Unknown company facts are intentionally not converted into claims.</p>
        <div class="proof">
          <div class="proof-row"><span class="status status--visible">VISIBLE</span><strong>Cutting tables and equipment in the supplied image</strong></div>
          <div class="proof-row"><span class="status">SUPPORTED</span><strong>Sample review before bulk manufacturing</strong></div>
          <div class="proof-row"><span class="status">SUPPORTED</span><strong>Production and packing reference updates</strong></div>
          <div class="proof-row"><span class="status">PENDING</span><strong>Verified location, capacity, equipment, and compliance data</strong></div>
        </div>
        <a class="link" href="/production/">Review production information</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 7 MATERIAL TO PACK-OUT ============ -->
<section class="section band-alt" data-od-id="manufacturing-capabilities">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="cap-grid">
      <div class="cap-intro" data-reveal>
        <p class="label">Material to pack-out</p>
        <h2>The details that shape the final garment.</h2>
        <p class="lead">Decisions are reviewed as a connected product system. A fabric choice affects fit, decoration, workmanship, care information, and packing, not just handfeel.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cap-ledger">
        <article class="cap-item" data-reveal>
          <span class="cap-flag">01 / FABRICS</span>
          <h3>Material direction</h3>
          <p>Review product use, composition, weight, color, handfeel, stretch, drape, and special material requirements.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Fleece and French terry</li>
            <li>Jersey and cotton options</li>
            <li>Woven shell and lining</li>
            <li>Stretch and performance options</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="cap-item" data-reveal>
          <span class="cap-flag">02 / WORKMANSHIP</span>
          <h3>Construction</h3>
          <p>Translate the silhouette into measurements, seams, pockets, closures, reinforcement, lining, and finishing instructions.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Fit and size review</li>
            <li>Stitching and seam details</li>
            <li>Pockets and reinforcement</li>
            <li>Buttons, zippers, and drawcords</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="cap-item" data-reveal>
          <span class="cap-flag">03 / DECORATION</span>
          <h3>Brand application</h3>
          <p>Match the decoration method and artwork placement to the garment, fabric, intended look, and order plan.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Screen printing</li>
            <li>Heat transfer</li>
            <li>Embroidery</li>
            <li>Patches and artwork placement</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="cap-item" data-reveal>
          <span class="cap-flag">04 / PRIVATE LABEL</span>
          <h3>Finishing system</h3>
          <p>Coordinate the visible and hidden brand details before packing instructions are finalized.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Woven, neck, size, and care labels</li>
            <li>Hangtags, stickers, and barcodes</li>
            <li>Polybags and folding rules</li>
            <li>Carton labels and marks</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 8 QUALITY CONTROL ============ -->
<section class="section band-dark" data-od-id="quality-control">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="qc-grid">
      <div class="qc-intro" data-reveal>
        <p class="label label--onDark">Quality control</p>
        <h2>Know what should be checked before the order ships.</h2>
        <p class="lead">Quality control should be understandable to a buyer working remotely. The checkpoints below focus on fit, appearance, branding, packing, and consistency with the approved product reference.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="qc-ledger">
        <article class="qc-item" data-reveal>
          <span class="qc-num">01</span>
          <div><h3>Incoming material reference</h3><p>Confirm fabric direction, color references, trims, and order details before cutting and assembly.</p></div>
        </article>
        <article class="qc-item" data-reveal>
          <span class="qc-num">02</span>
          <div><h3>In-process workmanship</h3><p>Review construction, measurements, stitching, placement, and visible issues while corrections can still be made.</p></div>
        </article>
        <article class="qc-item" data-reveal>
          <span class="qc-num">03</span>
          <div><h3>Finished garment check</h3><p>Compare fit, appearance, labeling, decoration, and key measurements with the approved sample and order notes.</p></div>
        </article>
        <article class="qc-item" data-reveal>
          <span class="qc-num">04</span>
          <div><h3>Pack-out verification</h3><p>Check label accuracy, folding, polybags, carton information, packing count, and requested reference photography.</p></div>
        </article>
        <article class="qc-item" data-reveal>
          <span class="qc-num">05</span>
          <div><h3>Shipment preparation</h3><p>Align carton details and shipment document support with the buyer's delivery plan before goods leave production.</p></div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 9 PACKAGING AND DELIVERY ============ -->
<section class="section" data-od-id="packaging-delivery">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="pack-grid">
      <div class="pack-main" data-reveal>
        <p class="label">Packaging and delivery</p>
        <h2>Prepare the order for the buyer's next handoff.</h2>
        <p class="lead">The delivery workflow begins before cartons are closed. Share the destination, target timing, warehouse or retail requirements, and the documents your receiving team expects.</p>
        <div class="pack-steps">
          <article class="pack-step">
            <span class="label">01 / BRAND</span>
            <h3>Labels and tags</h3>
            <p>Confirm label files, care information, size identification, hangtags, stickers, and barcodes.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="pack-step">
            <span class="label">02 / UNIT</span>
            <h3>Fold and bag</h3>
            <p>Define folding, polybag, insert, sticker, and presentation requirements for each unit.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="pack-step">
            <span class="label">03 / CARTON</span>
            <h3>Pack-out</h3>
            <p>Specify carton marks, product mix, size breakdown, packing count, and handling notes.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="pack-step">
            <span class="label">04 / HANDOFF</span>
            <h3>Shipment support</h3>
            <p>Review packing references, carton information, destination details, and requested document support.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
      <aside class="pack-note" data-reveal>
        <span class="label">Planning note</span>
        <h3>No fixed delivery promise without an order review.</h3>
        <p><strong>Final timing and shipping method depend on the confirmed product, materials, quantity, packaging, destination, and buyer requirements.</strong></p>
        <p>Include the target market, destination, deadline, and packing or document needs in the initial inquiry so the delivery path can be assessed with the product plan.</p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 10 INQUIRY ============ -->
<section class="section band-alt" data-od-id="inquiry-conversion">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="inq-grid">
      <div class="inq-left" data-reveal>
        <p class="label">Start the conversation</p>
        <h2>Send enough detail to get a useful manufacturing review.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="inq-right" data-reveal>
        <div class="inq-ledger" aria-label="Recommended inquiry details">
          <span>Product category</span>
          <span>Estimated quantity</span>
          <span>Tech pack or references</span>
          <span>Fabric target</span>
          <span>Size range and fit</span>
          <span>Branding files</span>
          <span>Packaging needs</span>
          <span>Destination and timing</span>
        </div>
        <div class="inq-actions">
          <a class="button button--dark" href="/contact-us/">Send project details</a>
          <a class="link" href="/production/">Review production first</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</EditorialLayout>
